  col
    h3 Two-Day Aerospace Festival
    h2 MAX POWER
    text Celebrate the spirit of American innovation at MAX POWER—an exposition of air and space technologies at Kennedy Space Center in Florida, Nov. 7-8.
    text The two-day event will feature immersive experiences for all ages to enjoy, including air shows, technology demonstrations, spaceflight hardware, military aircraft, and behind‑the‑scenes access to America’s spaceport.In collaboration with Air Dot Show, UP Summit, Space Florida, Delaware North, and Purpose Entertainment, MAX POWER blends history, exploration, and the cutting edge of aerospace into an unforgettable experience.
    link "Learn More about MAX POWER" https://www.nasa.gov/maxpower/
  col
    image https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/AFRC2026-0146-13/AFRC2026-0146-13~large.jpg?w=1920&h=1280&fit=clip&crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint "A red, white, and blue NASA F‑15 is shown beside another jet aircraft during a cross‑country flight. The full F‑15 is visible, while only a portion of the F/A‑18’s red‑and‑white wing appears in the frame."
    text A NASA F‑15 aircraft is shown flying next to a NASA F/A‑18 during a cross‑country flight from Spokane, Washington, to Washington, D.C., on July 2, 2026.
    text NASA/Jim Ross
